'' A '.rc' IS COMPILED AND LINKED, and before this it was compiled as FreeBASIC.
'' That did not even fail: 'STRINGTABLE BEGIN 101, "text" END' is identifiers and a
'' string literal, which parse as statements -- so the program built, the resource
'' was silently absent, and nothing said so. An icon or a version block would have
'' gone missing from a shipped binary with no diagnostic anywhere.
''
'' llvm-rc, NOT GoRC. fbc runs GoRC.exe out of its own bin/ and asks for a COFF
'' object; llvm-rc ships with the LLVM install tiko already requires and produces a
'' .res, which lld-link consumes directly. Same .rsrc section, one less external
'' tool -- checked: the built exe has one.
''
'' The '.res' is an intermediate and is deleted after the link, so only the exe is
'' asserted here. The '.rc' is the user's and is never touched.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/res.bas tests/driver/src/res.rc -o tests/driver/res.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/res.exe
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: tests/driver/src/res.res
